We have been using YARN successfully, although not extensively in production.  If you would like to try it out, you can either get the following: Rhipe_0.75.0_cdh5mr2.tar.gz <http://ml.stat.purdue.edu/rhipebin/Rhipe_0.75.0_cdh5mr2.tar.gz> built against cdh5, or clone our dev branch and build it: https://github.com/tesseradata/RHIPE/tree/dev.  We are actively working on this branch and plan to exclusively support YARN from this version on.  Let us know if you have any questions.

